course: dictionary
lesson: 9130
title: Snack
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A snack is a small amount of food you eat between meals. «A banana is a good snack» tells you a snack is something small, not a whole meal.
explain: Snack can also be a verb. To snack is to eat a snack, so you snack on fruit or nuts. The forms are snack, snacks, snacked and snacking, as in «We snacked on nuts in the car».
explain: The word can also show up in real life. «You carry water, a snack, a warm or waterproof layer and a whistle» on a hill walk, because you may need energy part-way and the weather can change.
fact: A snack is a small amount of food eaten between meals.
fact: Snack can be a noun («a snack») or a verb («to snack», «snacked», «snacking»).
fact: Healthy snacks include fruit, nuts and yogurt.
fact: Sharing snacks equally between children is a division problem.
fact: Snack time, a snack bar and an after-school snack are everyday uses of the word.
exercise: What is a snack? | A big meal eaten late at night | A sport played in the hills | *A small amount of food eaten between meals | A drink of water only
exercise: In «We snacked on nuts in the car», what kind of word is snacked? | *A verb | An adjective | A noun
exercise: Mia has 12 snacks to share equally between 3 children. How many does each child get? | 5 | 9 | 3 | *4
test: Which food is a healthy snack? | Sweets | *Yogurt | Crisps | Fizzy cola
test: «You carry water, a snack, a warm layer and a whistle» on a hill walk. Why is a snack in the pack? | To wear as a hat | To scare away birds | To make the pack heavier | *To keep you going if you get hungry on the walk
exam: Which sentence uses snack as a verb? | The snack bar was closed. | A cold snack sat on the table. | *We snacked on nuts in the car.
